d stories and check that both are stored and the\n    neighbour's score is a positive `Decimal`;\n  - send two publishes through `handler()` and expect 201 both times;\n  - unit-test `to_dynamo()` on nested floats, and check that ints and bools\n    are left alone.\n\n  The fake table already rejects floats the same way boto3 does, so these\n  tests fail on the old code (verified: 1 failure and 2 errors) and pass with\n  the fix (`python3 -m unittest discover tests` → 4 OK).\n\n## Related, not changed\n\n- `table.scan()` reads only the first 1 MB page (it ignores `LastEvaluatedKey`),\n  and it does a full scan on every publish. Once the library grows, `similar`\n  will quietly miss stories and publishing will slow down.\n- An API key appears in plain text in `README.md`, and an API token in\n  plain text in `samconfig.toml`. Both files are committed. Consider rotating\n  them and moving them to a secret store.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016xLjmHLznsNVhyS9mxMqUd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdJCXQrtNKUZW8tQyt6h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the 500 on the second publish. The tests pass, and the cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Cause:** each story is saved together with its most similar existing stories, and each of those has a similarity score that is a Python `float`. The library that writes to DynamoDB rejects floats (\"Float types are not supported\"), so saving fails and the handler returns 500. The first publish worked only because the table was empty, so the list of similar stories was `[]` and held no floats. Every publish after that has at least one similar story, so it fails. This matches `logs/error.log` exactly: one 201, then 500s at `put_item`. The existing test only ever published one story into an empty table, so it never hit this.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **`src/app.py`:** a new `to_dynamo()` function turns every float in the item into a `Decimal`, and `publish()` runs it on the whole item just before saving. Because it covers the whole item and not just the score, a float field added later gets converted too instead of failing again.\n- **`tests/test_publish.py`:** new regression tests that publish two related stories (directly and through the handler, expecting 201 both times), plus a test of the conversion on nested values. The fake table already rejects floats the way the real one does.\n- **Tests:** the new tests fail on the old code (1 failure, 2 errors) and all 4 pass with the fix.\n\nI haven't committed anything, and nothing was deployed or sent anywhere.\n\nTwo things I noticed but didn't change (also noted in `ANSWER.md`):\n- **Missed stories:** each publish reads only the first 1 MB page of the table. Once the library grows, similar stories will be quietly missed and publishing will get slower.\n- **Exposed secrets:** an API key is in plain text in `README.md`, and an API token in `samconfig.toml`, both committed. They're worth rotating and moving to a secret store."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1030,"cache_read_input_tokens":26230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1030},"output_tokens":621,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c90fabef-d265-4cf4-b8ba-a1be6f917d70","uuid":"bfa109a8-c25f-407d-9b8e-d32705eab0ab","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:16:56.482Z","request_id":"req_011CgdJCXCif8Jy4hkVTsCkq"}
